<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ælfgifu of Northampton</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 990–after 1036</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ælfgifu of Northampton (c. 990–after 1036) was the first wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great">Cnut the Great</a> and mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-harefoot">Harold Harefoot</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Around 1030 Cnut sent her with their son Svein to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, but their regime became hated for its heavy taxes and new laws, while the cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Saint Olaf</a> grew. They were driven out in 1035, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-the-good">Magnus the Good</a> became king.</p></div>
